# docs/kernel-modules-allow — the declared shared-kernel surface (OI-48 ruled
# (d), 2026-08-21; executed WI-494).
#
# Read by project-trajectory/scripts/check_trajectory.py's
# `read_kernel_modules`. `cross_component_findings` treats an import edge
# whose DESTINATION is listed here as NOT A SEAM AT ALL — neither a hard
# finding nor the multi-membership advisory. A module below is consumed
# across components BY DESIGN: re-declaring that fact edge-by-edge (the
# WI-064 seam registry, OI-48's option (b)) would restate "everyone imports
# the shared helper" once per caller, which is the over-tracing the kit's
# proportionality doctrine (SN-012) already refuses elsewhere.
#
# THIS IS THE REUSE PROVISION OI-48 generalised into, not a kitlib special
# case: any future module whose real consumers span components takes this
# same declared path — one entry, one recorded reason — never a hardcoded
# name inside the checker. Each addition is a deliberate act; the
# multi-membership advisory (WI-440) keeps surfacing undeclared candidates
# so a future kernel does not hide behind a stale four-way `Component` tag
# the way this one did before OI-48.
#
# GRAMMAR, the docs/provenance-allow idiom: one non-blank, non-`#`-comment
# line per entry, `<module path> — <reason>` (an em dash, space each side).
# A REASON IS REQUIRED — unlike docs/if-tc-coverage-allow's migration seed,
# there is no bare-baseline exception here, because a kernel declaration is
# never a default (OI-41 ARM precedent: hard at birth). A line with no
# separator, or an empty module or reason on either side of it, DECLARES
# NOTHING: it grants no exemption (fail-safe — absence of a valid
# declaration means the seam rule still applies in full) and is reported by
# `kernel_allow_parse_findings` (WARN plain, ERROR under `--strict`, the
# `[checks] components_check` opt-out).
#
# ONE-DIRECTIONAL: exempting a destination never exempts that same module as
# a SOURCE. A kernel module importing a non-kernel sibling stays fully
# policed — kitlib's own case is additionally caught by a dedicated static
# test (tests/test_bootstrap.py, WI-448's bootstrap-manifest check), which
# this file does not replace.
#
# `project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/station.py` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
# Its one cross-component edge (scripts/traj_panels -> scripts/kitlib/station)
# is already declared and policed as IF-093, authored alongside LLR-182 for
# exactly this module so the edge stays a normal, scrutinized seam rather
# than an invisible kernel exemption — adding it here would silence an edge
# that was deliberately kept visible. Its `Component` tag stays `CMP-008`
# (LLR-182), unchanged by this ruling's execution: station.py's real
# consumer base is the lane-close machinery that component already owns,
# not general reuse across all four components the way config/git/registry/
# ladder/stage are.

